   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organization of a preparatory expert meeting and an overall concluding meeting early 2018 with a view to strengthen the functioning of the human rights treaty body system.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="268768" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Preparatory meeting - New Horizons: Enhancing impact and envisaging new methods of work, Copenhagen 01/2018
- Concluding meeting - Towards a 21st Century Treaty Body System, Wilton Park, UK 02/2018</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Successful organization of the 2 meetings with an aim to provide inputs to the Secretary General&apos;s report to the General Assembly in 2018"></target>
     <actual value="- A preparatory expert meeting held in Copenhagen on the 9-10 January 2018. The participants included TB members. experts and representatives from States and NHRIs. The core ideas and discussion were summarized in the outcome document (Idea Catalogue) of the meeting that was preparatory to the discussions at the concluding meeting at Wilton Park.
- A concluding meeting at Wilton Park held on the 28 February &#x2013; 2 March 2018. The participants included TB members. experts and representatives from OHCHR. States and NHRIs. A detailed summary of the meeting was summarised in the Wilton Park report."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
